The amount of dynamic memory is a feature of your hardware and software
configuration.  memory.size() just reports what is being used, so it
makes no different.  The default is to allow the S session to use as much
memory as available, so you are probably at the limits of your system
configuration and would have to free space used by other programs, add
some memory, or expand the allocation of swap space.

