Hello members!

I have generated 90 plots in .jpg format, now I need to print them out 6 
per page (total 15 pages), the plot must appear randomly. I will need to 
make 20 to 30 prints; of course each copy is randomized. I will also need 
to log the sequence of appearance for each printing. Can I do this in S?

For your reference, I attached my codes for generating the plots. I wrote 
and ran in R. I figure (and hope) that doesn.t make difference in S.

Thanks for any input!

Jindan

options("digits"=2)

#Specify process standard deviation
for (i in c(1,3,5)) {

#Specify the magnitude of out-of-control points
for (j in c(1.5, 2.0, 2.5, 3.0, 3.5, 4.0)) {

#generate replication
for (k in 1:5) {

#Generate data
rnorm(24) -> x
j -> x[25]
1:25 -> idx
abs(round(x/i, 2)) -> magnitude
matrix(c(x, idx, magnitude), ncol=3) -> z

#Randomize data
z[sample(25),] -> z

#Plot chart on .png file
png(filename=paste("std_", i, "_","mag_", j, "_", "no_", k, ".png", 
sep=""), width=480, height=480, pointsize=12,bg="white")
plot(z[,1], type="o", ylab="x-bar",,xlab="Sample 
number",ylim=c(-3.5,3.5),axes=F)
title(main="Shewhart control chart without UCL and LCL", 
sub=paste("Process Standard Deviation = ", i))
box()
axis(1)
abline(h=0)
text(y=z[,1],seq(along=x), adj=1.3,cex=0.8)
dev.off()

#Write data on .txt file

write(t(z), file=paste("std_", i, "_","mag_", j, "_", "no_", k, 
".txt"),ncolumns=3)
}
}       
}

