We did find the solution to the problem some users have found while
trying to use Connect C++ with Visual C++.NET.

The problem is the .NET compiler conflicts with _declspec(dllimport) 
decorations on template class declarations.  

Attached is a modified version of one of the header files we provide in the 
sconnect directory in S-PLUS 6.1 or higher.  Please replace the attached
header file spdefs.h with the attached version.

First, create a backup copy of your spdefs.h in the sconnect directory. 
The default location for spdefs.h is:

C:\Program Files\splus61\sconnect\spdefs.h
 
Then replace the existing file with the attached version of spdefs.h.
 
When you compile your Visual C++ .NET project using sconnect.h, the _MSC_VER is 
>= 1300.  
Then the symbol SCONNECT_LIB_EXTERN becomes undefined.  When this macro is 
undefined,
the compiler errors are eliminated because all the template classes in the 
other headers then 
lose the _declspec(dllimport) decoration.
 
This workaround will be implemented in our next released version of S-PLUS for 
Windows.

Please let me know if you have any questions or additional problems.

Sincerely,

