data.dump(oldStyle=T) should help.  It is the case though that some objects
created under S-PLUS 5/6 can't be reproduced under S+2000.  This is the
case for objects with S4-classes, for example, although
data.dump(oldStyle=T) may have a stab at them.

We haven't found this much of a problem (if oldStyle=T is used), but the
long-term solution is to use S+6.1 everywhere, as that has a common base
across all platforms.

