Subject: Mantel-Haenszel analysis
Message-ID: <sdd4d194.095@s-webmail.lshtm.ac.uk>

S+ has the function 'mantelhaen.test' which, in epidemiological terms, tests 
for an association between an exposure and an outcome, stratifying on a 
possible confounder.  This function produces the chi-squared and p value.  It 
would be useful to have, in addition, the crude (unadjusted) odds ratio, the 
stratum-specific odds ratios, the M-H summary odds ratio (a weighted average of 
the stratum ORs), the CI for the M-H OR, and a test for interaction.  Is anyone 
aware of such a function (whether or not based on the built-in one), either 
public domain or which you would be willing to share?  Thanks, Neal

